ian  or lagrangian actually has an implicit  form for example the double pendulum's  euler lagrangian equation has an  implicit form so when we simulate the  double pendulum and building the correct  libraries we find out the cindy pie can  figure out the correct physical loss  that's hidden beneath this data set and  in this case the cindy pi correctly  identified all the lagrangian equation  from the from the simulation data of  double pendulum  okay  now in summary we did develop a new  algorithm called zindipi this algorithm  can parallelly solve for implicit or  rational problem and moreover it is more  noise robust and requires less data  point  finally it can identify physical laws  from the data  if you're interested in other  papers please feel free to check it out  and if you want to use cindy pi for your  research at work please also check out  the packages below  and i would like to thank my  collaborators professor steve ronton and  professor nissan quits at university of  washington and thank you all for  listening

